{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And you shall not flatter the land.</b> The explanation of the matter is thus: the earth is likened to one who has opened her mouth without limit to swallow everything upon her, as it is said (Isaiah 5:14): ״לָכֵן הִרְחִיבָה שְׁאוֹל נַפְשָׁהּ וּפָעֲרָה פִיהָ לִבְלִי חֹק״ — 'Therefore Sheol has enlarged her desire, and opened her mouth without limit,' etc. — and it is written (Proverbs 30:16): ״אֶרֶץ לֹא שָׂבְעָה מַּיִם״ — 'the earth that is not sated with water.' For in truth the earth is never sated, and the wicked who commit murder flatter the earth by giving it something to swallow; and this is חֲנֻפָּה (flattery/hypocrisy), for anyone who gives something to one who is unworthy of it, in order that he in turn will come and give him something in return — this is called חֲנֻפָּה. And so too the matter whereby the earth flatters the wicked by giving them its yield for all their needs, which from the earth have their source, and likewise a place to dwell and to establish themselves upon it, even though the wicked are not worthy of any of this — as it is said (Isaiah 24:5): ״וְהָאָרֶץ חָנְפָה תַּחַת יוֹשְׁבֶיהָ״ — 'And the earth is polluted [flattered] under its inhabitants.'" "And this is what it says: ״כִּי הַדָּם יַחֲנִיף אֶת הָאָרֶץ״ — 'for the blood flatters the earth' — for the wicked one gives it blood to swallow, so that the earth will in exchange give him its grain and its fat; therefore it shall not be atoned for the earth except by the blood of him who shed it. And this atonement is for the fact that it sustained the murderer even for a single moment, for flattery is accounted to it in this matter, and they would say that both of them flatter each other. And the reason Cain was not killed was for the sake of the settlement of the world, for he was alone in the world. Nevertheless, the earth removed itself from this suspicion: it caused a thorn and thistle to sprout for him, and he became a fugitive and a wanderer on the earth — and if so, it no longer gave him the two kinds of benefit that he had from the earth. And even this was on the side of kindness toward Cain specifically, as stated; but for all generations it shall not be atoned for except by the blood of him who shed it, to remove it from the state of this flattery."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:07.543468087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}